(findings . ((lint-split-scope . ".github/workflows/ci.yml at implementation-sha: job lint runs only Protected governance controller tests and Workflow YAML validation — none of setup-racket, scripts/lint-all.rkt, check-version-expectations, check-lint-alignment, or classify-metadata appear in its steps; job lint-quality carries the full Racket lint suite (scripts/lint-all.rkt, check-version-expectations, check-lint-alignment, metadata-inventory as artifact, metadata-lint blocking) and has no downstream needs, so heavyweight lint is off the PR critical path")
             (policy-and-pins . "scripts/required-pr-checks.policy contains both lint and lint-quality (and not lint-alignment); scripts/gsd-gates/gate-claims.rkt ci-required-jobs exposes the same set and tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt evaluates it live — the split is pinned against the real sources of truth, not copies; no orphaned job-set pin exists anywhere in the repo (every pin updated in the same commit series)")
             (fail-closed-integrity . "tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt asserts lint stays required throughout the split (fail-closed) and tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt pins required-set == policy contents with the named two-sided drift alarm; at no point in the applied sequence is lint unrequired, and lint-quality becomes required in the same atomic change that adds it to the workflow")
             (dag-checkpoint-honesty . "artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w1/dag-checkpoint.json pairs before and after at the SAME head SHA c6ee39e4…: before is the measured W0 baseline run, after is the derived shape projection under the split topology; the record is labeled topology checkpoint — not a cohort in two places and the tests (31/31 green) enforce the pairing, per-job started_at/completed_at completeness, and that after's lint completes before test (0) starts")
             (critical-path-claim-substantiated . "the projection shows lint dropping its ~3m33s of Racket steps so it completes before fast-env/test start, and lint-quality running in parallel with no consumers — the critical-path improvement claim is a structural consequence of the needs-graph, not an extrapolated timing guess")
             (rollback-order . "the validation record fixes the revert order (unrequire lint-quality first, then restore workflow/policy, lint required throughout) and names a half-reverted or fail-open state as a release blocker — matches §7 W1 item 5")
             (attempt-history . "attempt-1's provider/network infra stop is recorded honestly; the committed work was resumed and extended (notably: the w9 harness is now anchored to its own file location so the declared `racket tests/...` invocation and `raco test` resolve identically — a robustness fix, not a behavior change), not redone")))
(concerns . ((post-merge-steps-open . "the §7.1 tail — lint-quality reporting green on main BEFORE the branch-protection requirement is added, then both verified required via the GitHub API — is intentionally outside this record's claims; it is coordinator-owned and must land while the wave issue is still open; the DAG checkpoint's API-snapshot requirement is satisfied for the pre-merge side by the W0 baseline and must be re-snapshotted by the coordinator post-merge")))
(record-only . "this review adds no code and touches no digest input")
